# libretranslate
msgid "**Breaking Changes:** Migration from *util-* to bundle inventories under *inventories/bundles/*; deployments must migrate to new bundle and role names. Central package and AUR model via *SYS_PACKAGES* and *SYS_AUR_PACKAGES*; new roles *sys-aur* and *sys-aur-install*; renames including *util-desk-dev-core* to *dev-core*, *util-desk-dev-python* to *dev-python*, *util-desk-dev-arduino* to *dev-arduino*; *util-srv-corporate-identity* removed."
msgstr "**Cambios de ruptura:** Migracións de *util-* Inventarios en *inventores/bundos/*As implementacións deben migrar a novos paquetes e nomes de roles. Paquete central e modelo AUR *SYS_PACKAGES* e *SYS_AUR_PACKAGES*Novos roles *sys-aur* e *sys-aur-install*Renomes incluídos *util-desk-dev-core* para *dev-core*, *util-desk-dev-python* para *dev-python*, *util-desk-dev-arduino* para *dev-arduino*; *Identidade corporativa util-srv* Retirado."

# libretranslate
msgid "**Bridges are explicit and validated.** When an addon itself integrates with another role, it MUST list the bridged service key under `bridges:`. Each listed key MUST resolve to a service block already declared in the same role's `meta/services.yml`. Lint fails otherwise. Front-door auth gates such as oauth2-proxy are not addon bridges unless the addon itself talks to that service. **Two distinct meanings of \"bridge\" exist and MUST NOT be conflated:** the `bridges:` *field* names an in-repo cross-role service dependency (e.g. an addon that talks to `svc-db-openldap`), whereas `mechanism: bridge` marks an addon that *is* a network/appservice bridge to an external system (e.g. a Matrix mautrix bridge to WhatsApp/Telegram). A single addon MAY be both: a `mechanism: bridge` addon MAY also declare a `bridges:` dependency on an in-repo service it relies on."
msgstr "**As pontes son explícitas e válidas.** Cando un addon se integra con outro papel, ten que listar a clave de servizo ponte baixo `bridges:`. Cada clave enumerada debe resolverse a un bloque de servizo xa declarado na mesma función. `meta/services.yml`. Lint falla doutra maneira. Portas de entrada como o auth2Non son pontes de addon a menos que o propio addon fale con ese servizo. **Dous significados diferentes \"bridge\" Existen e non se deben confundir:** El `bridges:` *Campo* Dependencia de servizo cross-role in-repo (un complemento que fala de `svc-db-openldap`), mentres que `mechanism: bridge` un complemento que *Está* Unha ponte de rede / servizo a un sistema externo (e.g. a Matrix A ponte mautrix para WhatsApp / Telegram)Un único addon pode ser ambos: a `mechanism: bridge` Tamén pode declarar a `bridges:` Dependencia dun servizo de rede en que depende."

