# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**Vía Oauth2Proxectando autoprovisionamento:** V1 todas as portas de acceso a través do cliente Keycloak OIDC compartido (Oauth2Proxy Edge). A apertura abrevia a identidade autenticada para n8como un fiador `Remote-Email` cabeceira (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); a `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` Guión (`files/hooks.js`, adaptado de [PavelSozonov/n8n-comunidade-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) Lee esa cabeceira, autoprovisiona un n local8n usuario no primeiro sinal e números n8cookie de sesión propia – así que cada usuario de Keycloak aterra directamente no editor de fluxo de traballo, sen segundo, n8Paso de login local."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**Vía Oauth2Proxectando autoprovisionamento:** V1 todas as portas de acceso a través do cliente Keycloak OIDC compartido (Oauth2Proxy Edge). A apertura abrevia a identidade autenticada para n8como un fiador ``Remote-Email`` cabeceira (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); a ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` Guión (``files/hooks.js``, adaptado de `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) Lee esa cabeceira, autoprovisiona un n local8n usuario no primeiro sinal e números n8cookie de sesión propia — así que cada usuario de Keycloak aterra directamente no editor de fluxo de traballo, sen segundo, n8Paso de login local."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** é o login de SAML de SuiteCRM contra Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` En [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml))Non hai un proxy diante. As solicitudes non autenticadas golpean o punto de entrada SAML do firewall de Symfony, que redirixe a Keycloak; a afirmación volve ao punto de entrada do firewall de Symfony. `/saml/acs` e establece unha sesión SuiteCRM real, polo que a aplicación fai a súa propia UI autenticada, incluíndo o seu control de logotipo. As contas créanse no primeiro login desde a afirmación (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), eo certificado de sinatura do IdP é lido a partir do descriptor do reino de Keycloak por [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) no arranque, sobre o proxy TorOCKS sempre que o emisor sexa unha cebola, porque `.onion` O emisor é directamente insoluble. `/auth` permanece accesible como o login de break-glass local."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** é o login de SAML de SuiteCRM contra Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` En ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` permanece accesible como o login de break-glass local."

