# libretranslate
msgid "By default — for an **untrusted** fork PR — the privileged `pull_request_target` build checks out the **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) from the base repository: the PR's changes merged onto base, with all workflow and build-orchestration scripts coming from base, never from the fork. Because `actions/checkout` otherwise refuses to fetch a PR ref under `pull_request_target`, the source checkout sets `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. The untrusted build runs **without organization secrets** — `secrets: inherit` is not passed and it authenticates to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN` only, so a malicious fork cannot read repository/organization secrets. (The `pull_request_target` token still carries `packages: write`, so the `🛡️ Trusted` label remains the real trust boundary for anything beyond image publication.)"
msgstr "Por defecto, para un **Desconfiados** Fort PR, o privilexiado `pull_request_target` Crea o check out **base merge ref** (`refs/pull/<N>/merge`) Desde o repositorio base: os cambios de PR fusionáronse na base, con todos os scripts de fluxo de traballo e de configuración de bases, nunca desde a base. Porque porque `actions/checkout` En caso contrario, négase a buscar un ref de PR `pull_request_target`O checkout fonte `allow-unsafe-pr-checkout: true`. A construción non confiada corre **Sen segredos de organización** - `secrets: inherit` Non se transmite e auténtrase ao GHCR coa per-job. `GITHUB_TOKEN` Só unha gark maliciosa non pode ler os segredos dos repositorios. (El `pull_request_target` Token aínda leva `packages: write`, Así, o `🛡️ Trusted` A etiqueta segue sendo o verdadeiro límite de confianza para calquera cousa máis aló da publicación da imaxe.)"

