msgid "The SSO (`sociallogin`) and LDAP (`user_ldap`) login surfaces are covered by the OIDC/LDAP Playwright specs (requirements 017/018)."
msgstr "O SSO (`sociallogin`) En LDAP (`user_ldap`) As superficies de login están cubertas polas especificacións OIDC/LDAP Playwright. (Requisitos 017/018)."

# libretranslate
msgid "The SSO back-channel pin, added automatically. On an onion deployment the OIDC endpoints handed to an application are public ``.onion`` authorities. That is right for the browser, which reaches them through Tor, but unroutable for the application's own server-side calls (code-to-token exchange, JWKS, userinfo): a container resolves ``.onion`` through Tor's resolver, not through DNS. Pinning the provider to a reachable address sends those calls over the local network to the proxy that already serves the vhost. Skipped unless the application has SSO enabled and the provider vhost is an ``.onion`` name, so it is a no-op on clearnet."
msgstr "O sSO back-channel pin, engadido automaticamente. Nun despregamento de cebola, os puntos finais do OIDC que se entregan a unha solicitude son públicos. ``.onion`` autoridades. Isto é certo para o navegador, que chega a eles a través de Tor, pero non é enrutable para as chamadas do lado do servidor da aplicación. (cambio de código a ficha, JWKS, userinfo): Un contenedor resolve ``.onion`` A través da resolución de Tor, non a través do DNS. Pinning o provedor para un enderezo accesible envía esas chamadas a través da rede local para o proxy que xa serve o servidor. Esquivado a menos que a aplicación teña SSO activado eo servidor servidor é un ``.onion`` Por iso, é un non-op en liña."

# libretranslate
msgid "The Sphinx configuration, extensions and generators live in [web-app-docs](../../roles/web-app-docs/). Deploy that role to build and serve the site."
msgstr "A configuración, extensións e xeradores de esfinxe viven en [web-app-docs](../../roles/web-app-docs/). Despregue ese papel para construír e servir o sitio."

# libretranslate
