# libretranslate
msgid "The `.onion` is a **deploy-time input**: a CLI helper mints the v3 key offline during inventory build, vaults it, and sets `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. It must NOT be a runtime fact — `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` is consumed at build time (LDAP base, CA, applications cache). The role restores the minted key into the hidden-service volume before Tor starts."
msgstr "El `.onion` É a **Use-time input**Un axudante de CLI minte o v3 clave offline durante a construción de inventario, muda-lo, e conxuntos `DOMAIN_PRIMARY`. Non debe ser un feito precipitado - `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` consumido no tempo de construción (base LDAP, CA, caché de aplicacións). O papel restablece a chave acuñada no volume oculto do servizo antes do inicio da Tor."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `@playwright/test` version pinned into the rendered `package.json` comes from `playwright.version` in `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` via the `image_version` filter. That YAML value is the single source of truth for the Playwright version."
msgstr "El `@playwright/test` Versión incluída no formato `package.json` vén de `playwright.version` En `roles/test-e2e-playwright/meta/services.yml` A través do `image_version` Filtros. Este valor YAML é a única fonte de verdade para a versión de Playwright."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `API.cloudflare.api_token` value (declared in `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, read via `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) must contain a valid Cloudflare API Token.   This token is used for all DNS operations and ACME (SSL/TLS certificate) challenges that require access to your Cloudflare-managed domains."
msgstr "El `API.cloudflare.api_token` Valor (Declarado en `group_vars/all/18_api.yml`, Ler vía `lookup('api', 'cloudflare.api_token')`) Debe conter unha nube válida API Token. Este token utilízase para todas as operacións de DNS e ACME. (Certificado SSL/TLS) Retos que requiren acceso aos dominios xestionados por Cloudflare."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow grants broad access to the `docker` CLI (alongside every other shell command) under the assumption that no production containers share the host. Non-mutating-image subcommands (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) can disrupt or destroy container state. Under test-only usage, the blast radius is bounded to ephemeral state that can be recreated from the compose stack."
msgstr "El `Bash(*)` permitir un amplo acceso á `docker` CLI (por todos os recantos,) Non hai contedores de produción que compartan o hóspede. Subcomandante de imaxes non mutantes (`rm`, `kill`, `stop`, `system prune`, `volume rm`, `cp`) Pode destruír ou destruír o estado dos contedores. Baixo o uso só de proba, o raio de explosión está ligado ao estado efémero que se pode recrear a partir da pila de composición."

# libretranslate
msgid "The `Bash(*)` allow lets the agent run any Makefile target without prompting. The `Makefile` is checked into git and reviewed on every pull request, so targets themselves are trusted. Every action a target performs still runs inside the sandbox."
msgstr "El `Bash(*)` Permite que o axente execute calquera obxectivo Makefile sen présa. El `Makefile` É comprobado en git e revisado en cada solicitude de tirar, polo que os propios obxectivos son de confianza. Cada acción que un obxectivo executa aínda corre dentro da caixa de area."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The `Corefile.tmpl` MUST be the source of truth. It is rendered to `Corefile` by [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), which substitutes its `${VAR}` placeholders in-process, using values from `.env` (generated from [default.env](../../default.env), overridable through the CLI's environment)."
msgstr "El `Corefile.tmpl` Debe ser a fonte da verdade. Está destinado a `Corefile` por [coredns.py](../../cli/administration/deploy/development/coredns.py), que substitúe a súa `${VAR}` Os interesados no proceso, utilizando valores de `.env` (xerado de [default.env](../../default.env), Sobreirable a través do entorno do CLI)."

# libretranslate
