# libretranslate
msgid "The swarm-test nfs-server serves shared storage from userspace `nfs-ganesha` (the `ganesha` flavor of `svc-storage-nfs-server`, the default in every runtime), which runs inside the privileged DinD node and never touches the host kernel `nfsd`, so an interrupted export cannot wedge the host. The `kernel` flavor is a per-inventory override for real hosts, where `nfsd` is not shared across clusters. If a swarm step ever hangs at `Reload NFS exports` from a stuck kernel-NFS mount, you MUST recover with `make swarm-clean` on the host (needs sudo): it removes what the docker CLI can, then runs `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. The no-sudo sandbox only prints those commands, so the host recovery is mandatory and the sweep MUST stop until it is done; never fall back to compose-only."
msgstr "O servidor nfs-test de swarm serve para almacenar o espazo de usuario. `nfs-ganesha` (El `ganesha` sabor de `svc-storage-nfs-server`, Por defecto en cada hora), que corre dentro do nodo DinD privilexiado e nunca toca o núcleo do servidor. `nfsd`, Así, unha exportación interrompida non pode evitar o hóspede. El `kernel` o sabor é un exceso de inventariación para os hóspedes reais, onde `nfsd` Non se comparte en grupos. Se un paso enxordece algunha vez `Reload NFS exports` dunha montaxe de kernel-NFS, cómpre recuperar `make swarm-clean` Sobre o hóspede (necesita sudo)elimina o que o docker CLI pode, entón corre `umount -f -l /var/lib/infinito` + `exportfs -ua` + `systemctl restart docker`. A caixa de area non-sudo só imprime os comandos, polo que a recuperación do servidor é obrigatoria e o varrido Debe parar ata que se fai; nunca volver caer só para compoñer."

