# libretranslate
msgid "This role installs the [sudo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) package and deploys a default sudoers file to ensure secure and consistent privilege escalation on the target system. It uses a preconfigured sudoers file that follows best practices and includes directives to read drop-in files from `/etc/sudoers.d`."
msgstr "Esta función instala o [Sudo](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudo) Paquete e desprega un ficheiro de sudoadores por defecto para garantir unha escalada de privilexios segura e consistente no sistema obxectivo. Usa un ficheiro de sudoadores preconfigurado que segue as mellores prácticas e inclúe directivas para ler ficheiros drop-in de `/etc/sudoers.d`."

# libretranslate
msgid "This role installs the ``baudolo`` CLI, lays out the on-host backup tree, deploys the systemd service that drives the periodic run, and wires the cleanup-of-failed-backups dependency so partial snapshots are not retained. Database seeding for individual apps is contributed by the consumer roles via ``tasks/03_seed-database-to-backup.yml``, which they include conditionally once ``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` is in ``group_names``."
msgstr "Esta función instala o ``baudolo`` CLI, establece a árbore de respaldo no servidor, desprega o servizo sistematizado que impulsa a execución periódica, e arame a dependencia de limpeza desfeitos, polo que as instantáneas parciais non se manteñen. A sementeira de bases de datos para aplicacións individuais é aportada polos roles dos consumidores. ``tasks/03_seed-database-to-backup.yml``, que inclúe unha vez ``svc-bkp-volume-2-local`` Está en ``group_names``."

# libretranslate
msgid "This role installs the `baudolo` CLI, lays out the on-host backup tree, deploys the systemd service that drives the periodic run, and wires the cleanup-of-failed-backups dependency so partial snapshots are not retained. Database seeding for individual apps is contributed by the consumer roles via `tasks/03_seed-database-to-backup.yml`, which they include conditionally once `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` is in `group_names`."
