# libretranslate
msgid "Trusted fork PRs: a maintainer-applied *trusted-pr* label runs a fork PR as deliberately released code — the orchestrator skips the fork-prerequisite wait and the privileged *pull_request_target* build switches its source from the base merge ref to the raw PR head, while the built image keeps the merge-SHA tag so every downstream consumer is unchanged. The label is the only switch (applying a label is collaborator-only on GitHub, so fork authors cannot grant it), build-orchestration scripts always come from the base repository, and both unlabeled fork PRs and same-repository PRs are untouched. See [the fork-PR pipeline](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) and [the contributor fork workflow](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."
msgstr "Fideicomiso PR: unha aplicación de mantemento *de confianza-pr* A etiqueta dirixe un fork PR como código deliberadamente liberado; o orquestrador salta a espera necesaria para a garfo e o privilexiado. *pull_request_target* build cambia a súa fonte da fusión base ref á cabeza de PR en bruto, mentres que a imaxe construída mantén a etiqueta de fusión-SHA polo que cada consumidor corrente abaixo non cambia. A etiqueta é o único interruptor. (Aplicando unha etiqueta só é colaborador en GitHub, polo que os autores de fork non poden concedela.), Os scripts de configuración sempre veñen do repositorio base, e as PRs fork non etiquetadas e PRs similares non se tocan. Ver [pipeline fork-PR](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pipeline.md) e [Colaborador fork workflow](docs/contributing/artefact/git/pull-request.md)."

