# libretranslate
msgid "What still blocks it is the transport. `server.py` speaks streamable HTTP upstream: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC to one URL and reads the reply, optionally SSE-framed. Baserow serves the older HTTP+SSE transport, where the client opens the stream and posts to the endpoint that stream announces — the shape `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` implements for `transport: sse` (\"the stream is the response channel and the endpoint it announces is the request channel\"). Fronting Baserow therefore needs that client transport in the adapter, or evidence that Baserow 2.3.3 also accepts a plain streamable-HTTP POST, which only a running instance can settle. A second consequence is waiting behind it: `web-app-n8n` speaks only `sse`, so it drops out of `allowed_consumers` the moment the surface becomes `streamable_http`."
msgstr "O que segue a ser o transporte. `server.py` Comentarios sobre HTTP upstream: `post_upstream` POSTS JSON-RPC para un URL e le a resposta, opcionalmente SSE-framed. Baserow serve ao máis antigo transporte HTTP+SSE, onde o cliente abre o fluxo e as mensaxes ao punto final que anuncia o fluxo. `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` Aplicacións para `transport: sse` (\"O fluxo é a canle de resposta e o punto final que anuncia é a canle de solicitude.\"). Fronte Baserow Polo tanto, é necesario o transporte do cliente no adaptador ou evidencia de que Baserow 2.3.3 Tamén acepta un POST-HTTP simple, que só unha instancia en execución pode resolver. Unha segunda consecuencia está detrás: `web-app-n8n` Só fala `sse`, Así que se desprende de `allowed_consumers` no momento en que a superficie se converte `streamable_http`."

