# libretranslate
msgid "When a host runs Docker Swarm with NFSv4-backed shared volumes (see [svc-storage-nfs-server](../svc-storage-nfs-server/) and [svc-storage-nfs-client](../svc-storage-nfs-client/)), this role **does not capture them** - provided some host is in the [svc-bkp-nfs-2-local](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/) inventory group. The lookup checks that group, not whether the role's last run actually succeeded, so a cluster whose export repository has never been deployed keeps that assumption unverified. The `backup_volume` lookup asks the same `swarm_nfs_backed()` predicate that drives the compose rewrite (`utils/storage/nfs.py`) and hands every export-backed volume to baudolo's `--volumes-no-backup-required`. Their single capture is then the export host's repository, which reads the same bytes from the server's own filesystem - no NFS round trip, no second copy racing the `link-dest` target."
msgstr "Cando un servidor corre Docker Swarm con NFSv4volume compartido (Ver [svc-storage-nfs-server](../svc-storage-nfs-server/) e [svc-storage-nfs-client](../svc-storage-nfs-client/))Este papel **Non os captura** Se algún servidor está en [svc-bkp-nfs-2-local](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/) Grupo de inventario. O lookup comproba que o grupo, non se a última execución realmente tivo éxito, polo que un cluster cuxo repositorio de exportación nunca foi implantado mantén esa suposición sen verificar. El `backup_volume` O PSOE pide o mesmo `swarm_nfs_backed()` predicado que dirixe a redacción (`utils/storage/nfs.py`) e entrega todos os volumes soportados por exportación para o baudolo `--volumes-no-backup-required`. A súa captura única é entón o repositorio do hóspede de exportación, que le os mesmos bytes do propio sistema de ficheiros do servidor, sen NFS, nin unha segunda copia correndo. `link-dest` Obxectivo."

# libretranslate
msgid "When a host runs Docker Swarm with NFSv4-backed shared volumes (see `svc-storage-nfs-server <../svc-storage-nfs-server/>`__ and `svc-storage-nfs-client <../svc-storage-nfs-client/>`__), this role **does not capture them** - provided some host is in the `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/>`__ inventory group. The lookup checks that group, not whether the role’s last run actually succeeded, so a cluster whose export repository has never been deployed keeps that assumption unverified. The ``backup_volume`` lookup asks the same ``swarm_nfs_backed()`` predicate that drives the compose rewrite (``utils/storage/nfs.py``) and hands every export-backed volume to baudolo’s ``--volumes-no-backup-required``. Their single capture is then the export host’s repository, which reads the same bytes from the server’s own filesystem - no NFS round trip, no second copy racing the ``link-dest`` target."
msgstr "Cando un servidor corre Docker Swarm con NFSv4volume compartido (Ver `svc-storage-nfs-server <../svc-storage-nfs-server/>`__ e `svc-storage-nfs-client <../svc-storage-nfs-client/>`__), Este papel **Non os captura** Se algún servidor está en `svc-bkp-nfs-2-local <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/>`__ Grupo de inventario. O lookup comproba que o grupo, non se a última execución realmente tivo éxito, polo que un cluster cuxo repositorio de exportación nunca foi implantado mantén esa suposición sen verificar. El ``backup_volume`` O PSOE pide o mesmo ``swarm_nfs_backed()`` predicado que dirixe a redacción (``utils/storage/nfs.py``) e entrega todos os volumes soportados por exportación ao baudolo ``--volumes-no-backup-required``. A súa única captura é entón o repositorio do hóspede de exportación, que le os mesmos bytes do propio sistema de ficheiros do servidor, sen NFS round trip, sen segunda copia competindo co servidor. ``link-dest`` Obxectivo."

# libretranslate
msgid "When a local deploy fails, you MUST validate the proposed fix inside a sidecar against the same image via `make compose-inner-run` (or `make compose-exec` against the live container) BEFORE starting another deploy, whenever the failure is reproducible there. The reproducible-there set includes: a container that crashes at startup, a misconfigured env var, an image-side bug, an in-container script that fails, or any failure whose root cause was traced to runtime state of the container. The only exception is failures that genuinely depend on multi-container or post-deploy state (network neighbours, persistent volumes, post-deploy Ansible hooks) — call that out explicitly in the iteration narrative."
msgstr "Cando unha implementación local falla, ten que validar a corrección proposta dentro dun sidecar contra a mesma imaxe. `make compose-inner-run` (ou `make compose-exec` Contra o contenedor vivo) Antes de iniciar outra implementación, sempre que o fracaso sexa reproducible alí. O conxunto reproducible-aquí inclúe: un recipiente que se estrela no arranque, unha var env mal configurada, un erro do lado da imaxe, un script que falla, ou calquera fallo cuxa causa raíz foi rastrexado para o estado de tempo de execución do contedor. A única excepción son os fallos que realmente dependen do estado multi-contido ou post-deploy. (veciños da rede, volumes persistentes, post-deploy Ansible ganchos) Isto explícase explicitamente na narración iterativa."

