# libretranslate
msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, which Snipe-IT matches against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "Cuando el outo2-proxy SSO é activo, nativo de Snipe-IT ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` Está habilitado a través do ``Setting`` Modelo (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``)Portas Nginx ``/login`` Vía Oauth2Proxy/Keycloak Inxectar o verificado ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` cabezallo, que xoga contra Snipe-IT ``users.username`` (O usuario debe pre-existir e ser activado, sincronizalos a través de LDAP.) para mintar un nativo ``snipeit_session``. Visitantes sen un usuario activado correspondente caen silenciosamente ata o formulario de login normal (ningún erro)O formulario de login contrasinal / LDAP permanece dispoñible como un recubrimento (``login_common_disabled = 0``), e o logout in-app é redirixido á URL central de sesión de OIDC."

