msgid "[ ] Compose and Swarm tests prove endpoint DNS/routing from each client and prove an adapter cannot reach unrelated application networks. **The isolation half is covered by the CLI test:** `run.sh` calls `isolation.sh` whenever `mcp.implementation` is `adapter`, and that reads from the engine which networks the sidecar is attached to and fails unless they are the role's own network plus the declared upstream one. `test_mcp_provider_cli_test.py` holds the test, so every enabled provider reaches it — a provider without a CLI test would also skip the isolation proof. What remains is the routing half: DNS resolution of each endpoint from each client, in both deploy modes, which only a running cluster can show."
msgstr "[ ] As probas de composición e Swarm proban o punto final de DNS/routing de cada cliente e proban que un adaptador non pode chegar a redes de aplicacións non relacionadas. **A metade do illamento está cuberto pola proba CLI:** `run.sh` chamadas `isolation.sh` Sempre `mcp.implementation` Está `adapter`, e que le a partir do motor que redes o sidecar está conectado e falla a menos que sexa a propia rede do rol máis a declarada augas arriba. `test_mcp_provider_cli_test.py` ten a proba, polo que cada provedor habilitado chega a el - un provedor sen unha proba de CLI tamén saltaría a proba de illamento. O que queda é a metade de enrutamento: resolución de DNS de cada punto final de cada cliente, en ambos os modos de implementación, que só pode mostrar un clúster en execución."

