msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`-) Dirixe a mesma viaxe e saltar na mesma bandeira."

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` e afirma que o provedor, a URL base e o modelo, polo que unha superficie non configurada non pode chegar a un despregamento verde."

# libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, unusable password) plus its own workspace, and binds the endpoint to that pair."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``contrasinal inutilizable) máis o seu propio espazo de traballo, e une o punto final a ese par."

# libretranslate
msgid "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` A persoa e as afirmacións basais funcionan incondicionalmente."

# libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` en cada variante."

# libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` En todas as variantes da matriz, porque a persoa colaboradora compartida non pode dirixir o sinal de calquera deles. Tres motivos independentes, cada un por si só:"

# libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: Contrato de fonte inmutable dun adaptador propiedade dun repositorio. ``category_allowlist`` adáptase a unha corrente ascendente que cambia as categorías enteiras e ofrece ningún filtro de per-tool, onde unha lista de permisos non sería aplicable. ``mcp_passthrough`` frontes un corrente ascendente que xa fala MCP en lugar de traducir REST. ``upstream_path`` Nomes que augas arriba onde vive no propio servidor da aplicación, para que o proxy poida ocultalo: chegar a ela camiña directamente por riba da lista de permisos que o adaptador existe para facer cumprir. Un provedor cuxa corrente ascendente é un sidecar separado declara ``upstream_network`` Non ten nada que ocultar alí."

# libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: Lista de alias DNS. Por defecto: ``[entity_name]`` Para shared_net, ``[]`` Para default_net"

# libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (Por defecto ``True``): o ficheiro (ou entrada dotted-path) Pode estar presente para un papel deste tipo. Set ``allowed: False`` Prohibir o ficheiro/entrada en roles deste tipo de modo que a capa de revestimento pode conter a ofensa cunha razón precisa."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` Só leva ``docker0`` Unha vez que se executa o daemon, e a configuración daemon escríbese antes que nun novo nodo - os feitos son recollidos no inicio do xogo, e nada os reúne despois da instalación. Ler o feito só, polo tanto, non produce nada na mesma dirección que ten que emitir o enderezo, o que deixa os recipientes internos apuntados no resoltor de pantalla eo control DNS DinD falla nun dominio só o nodo dnsmasq sabe."

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (Por defecto)"

# libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (Por defecto) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD)MDM corre70 Subroles augas arriba para entregar Synapse, Element, cada ponte soportada, Element Call e Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD por compromiso, fai un inventario MDAD ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, e desactiva o Traefik / Postgres / Redis Así, os servizos de Infinito de volta a pila."

# libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` O público S3 punto final e é posible sen o SSO."

# libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` é lido a partir das variables de xogo a menos que se indique como ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` que o Bloque en vez de ``ports``, Para Discourseficheiro de lanzamento, que ``expose:`` A lista é o que se converte ``docker run -p`` Aí."

# libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` O cliente fai o descubrimento."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: O Asistente de casa abarca o token á conta que a minou. Este despregue apóiao para o administrador, polo que unha chamada chega como o administrador que lle pediu ao cliente. A exposición de entidades aínda limita o seu alcance. Chegar ao servidor de ferramentas está conectado no papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC."

msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: El API Token é emitido contra a conta de administrador, polo que cada chamada leva os dereitos da conta, non importa quen pregunta ao cliente. Chegar ao servidor de ferramentas está regulado no papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC, que é unha concesión separada da administración. Jenkins."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: O token de acceso persoal está contra a ``root`` conta e almacenado en ``administrator`` Cada chamada leva os dereitos da conta, non importa quen pregunta ao cliente. Chegar ao servidor de ferramentas está regulado no papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC, que é unha concesión separada da administración. GitLab."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: O identificador de servizo web é emitido contra a conta de administrador, polo que unha chamada leva os dereitos desa conta independentemente de quen preguntou ao cliente. As funcións adxuntas só son lidas, o que limita o que estes dereitos poden facer aquí. Chegar ao servidor de ferramentas está regulado no papel ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Unha chamada chega a Baserow como propietario do punto final, independentemente de quen pediu ao cliente, e alcanza só o único espazo de traballo que posúe. Este é o segundo límite da lista de adaptadores, non un substituto."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``:: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` Grupo RBAC, que é unha subvención independente de manter a Nextcloud conta."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``- chamadas MCP de identidade executadas. ``user`` e ``oidc`` Ademais, require a ``delegation`` bloque, porque un portador de implantación renderizado é unha conta de servizo, non importa o que os metadatos reivindicacións."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` coa ficha dos datos do descubrimento"

# libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: Sistema de autenticación que garda o punto final."

# libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` é asesor e nunca falla a unidade; todo rexeitamento é rexistrado na revista ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, Así que comproba se un host que esperas facer fotos non. Un afirmado ``btrfs``/``zfs`` falla a unidade, que é o punto de indicala. Antes de cada instantánea o lanzador tamén elimina ``.baudolo-*`` Deixa atrás unha execución morto deixa dentro da raíz de datos."

# libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``:: ``cloud`` ou ``chezmoi``"

# libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (string): directorio base para ficheiros CA"

# libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` Pre-limpa o esquema nunha sesión psql e volve reproducir o dump na seguinte, polo que un consumidor que entra entre recrea o esquema e o replay morre por si mesmo. ``CREATE TABLE``. É dicir, o rexeitamento, mentres que o consumidor se nega."

# libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` Usando o centro MariaDB́s ``root`` Para crear o BD per-site en primeiro plano."

# libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` Nunca existo dentro EspoCRM Autoprovisionamento OIDC (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` As persoas corren en todas as variantes."

# libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` Indica o grao en que unha parella ao servizo declara: ``>= 1`` mantén o compañeiro no mesmo servidor, ``< 1`` Deixa que viva por si mesmo. O valor sitúase no lado do consumidor da relación, polo que a parella está dirixida e as dúas direccións dun par non deben estar de acordo."

# libretranslate
